                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="stats-box">
                    <h4>Normal Volume Days</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Count: <strong>{(~df['HighVolume']).sum():,}</strong> days</li>
                        <li>Avg Price Change: <strong>{df[~df['HighVolume']]['AbsPriceChange'].mean()*100:.3f}%</strong></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight">
                <strong>Liquidity Observation:</strong> High-volume days are associated with significantly larger price movements ({df[df['HighVolume']]['AbsPriceChange'].mean()*100:.3f}% vs {df[~df['HighVolume']]['AbsPriceChange'].mean()*100:.3f}%), confirming that volume and volatility are positively correlated. This has implications for position sizing and risk management during high-activity periods.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 6: Key Takeaways -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>6. Key Takeaways & Forward-Looking Considerations</h2>

            <div class="highlight" style="border-left-color: var(--blue);">
                <h3 style="color: var(--blue); margin-bottom: 15px;">Summary Statistics</h3>
                <ul style="margin-left: 20px;">
                    <li><strong>Total Return:</strong> {((last_close/first_close)-1)*100:.1f}% over {years:.1f} years</li>
                    <li><strong>Risk-Adjusted Performance:</strong> Sharpe-like ratio of {sharpe_like:.2f}</li>
                    <li><strong>Worst Case:</strong> {max_drawdown*100:.1f}% maximum drawdown</li>
                    <li><strong>Tail Risk:</strong> 1% VaR at {np.percentile(returns_clean, 1)*100:.2f}% daily loss</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h3>Volatility Regime Insights</h3>
            <ul style="margin-left: 20px; line-height: 2;">
                <li><strong>Low Vol Period:</strong> {low_vol_threshold*100:.1f}% annualized threshold – gold spends {(df['VolRegime']=='low').sum()/len(df)*100:.0f}% of time in this regime, typically during stable macroeconomic conditions.</li>
                <li><strong>High Vol Period:</strong> {high_vol_threshold*100:.1f}% annualized threshold – {len(crisis_periods):,} crisis days identified, predominantly during systemic stress events.</li>
                <li><strong>Current Regime:</strong> Last observed volatility at {df['RollingVol60'].iloc[-1]*100:.1f}% (annualized), currently classified as <strong>{df['VolRegime'].iloc[-1]}</strong>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Seasonal Considerations</h3>
"""

# Find best and worst months
monthly_means_df = df.groupby('Month')['LogReturn'].mean() * 100
best_month = monthly_means_df.idxmax()
worst_month = monthly_means_df.idxmin()
best_return = monthly_means_df.max()
worst_return = monthly_means_df.min()

html_content += f"""            <ul style="margin-left: 20px; line-height: 2;">
                <li><strong>Best Month:</strong> {month_names_list[best_month-1]} ({best_return:.2f}% annualized)</li>
                <li><strong>Worst Month:</strong> {month_names_list[worst_month-1]} ({worst_return:.2f}% annualized)</li>
